                  "resolution": null,
                  "resolution_audit": null
                },
                "stdout_tail": "{\"actual_models\": [\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\", \"claude-sonnet-5\"], \"selected_family_models\": [\"claude-sonnet-5\"], \"other_reported_models\": [\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"], \"verdict\": {\"findings\": [\"bootstrap_controller.rs: Controller::start validates that the parent Job has a non-zero timeout_seconds, but never bounds the caller-supplied `timeout: Duration` (used to compute controller_deadline) against the Job's remaining timeout budget. A caller could pass a `timeout` longer than the Job's own deadline, letting the native child's wait in `finish()` outlive the Job's finite-timeout guarantee that the primary-role check was meant to enforce.\", \"The task asks to check 'Linux and native success conjunction' (i.e., how the native Controller's exit status is combined with the Linux subject's outcome/seal), but neither provided file shows this logic: bootstrap_controller.rs only returns the native exit code from finish(), and cross_os_reset.rs's Subject only relays mailbox files (including seal.json) without any combination with a native result. No code evidencing this conjunction was supplied, so it cannot be confirmed as correctly implemented.\"], \"summary\": \"Reviewed bootstrap_controller.rs and cross_os_reset.rs. Primary-role/finite-timeout preflight, Job-containment (no breakaway), and narrow mailbox export are implemented as expected with concrete evidence. Two gaps found: the controller's own spawn timeout isn't validated against the Job's remaining timeout, and no code was provided showing how native and Linux success are conjoined.\\\"\", \"verdict\": \"findings\"}}\n",
